[0.000, "o", "\u001b[36muser\u001b[0m\r\nUse $activity-monitor to check my Mac's resource activity and explain what may be slowing it down.\r\n\r\n<stdin>\r\nSIMULATED CAPTURE (synthetic demo input, not from a real Mac)\r\nSymptom: typing lags and the fans are loud since this morning.\r\nHardware: 10-core Apple silicon laptop, 16 GB memory. Captured with: top -l 3 -s 5 -o cpu -n 8\r\n\r\nInterval 3 of 3\r\nLoad Avg: 9.81, 8.92, 7.40\r\nCPU usage: 71.20% user, 14.05% sys, 14.75% idle\r\nPhysMem: 15G used (2410M wired, 3105M compressor), 512M unused.\r\nVM: 1820(0) swapins, 41233(0) swapouts\r\nDisks: 9123441/210G read, 6012231/180G written\r\n\r\nPID    COMMAND          %CPU  TIME     MEM    STATE\r\n4211   node             312.4 48:12.55 2104M  running\r\n4198   Code Helper (Re  88.1  21:40.10 1650M  running\r\n612    WindowServer     34.7  95:22.01 410M   running\r\n3307   Google Chrome He 22.9  12:02.44 980M   sleeping\r\n1188   mds_stores       18.3  04:51.20 160M   running\r\n4402   Docker VM        12.0  33:10.90 4096M  running\r\n381    kernel_task      9.8   60:01.33 1"]
[0.000, "o", "2M    running\r\n2210   Slack Helper     3.1   02:11.05 420M   sleeping\r\n</stdin>"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[5.719, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mcodex\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\nI’m using the activity-monitor skill to assess your simulated capture and identify the most useful next check.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
